# File size & separation of concerns

- **Keep files small.** Split when a screen, hook, or util grows past a reasonable length (roughly ~150–200 lines). Prefer more small files over one large file.
- **UI screens/components (`*.tsx`):** Presentational only — JSX, light local UI state, calling hooks. No heavy business math, no fat inline data transforms.
- **Custom hooks (`hooks/use[Feature].ts` or feature-local `use*.ts`):** Stateful logic, side effects, store wiring, derived UI state.
- **Logic (`utils/`, later `services/`):** Pure helpers, calculations, formatting. No React imports.
- **Early returns** over nested `if/else`. **No `any`** — strict TypeScript. **DRY** — extract repeated UI into shared components.
